.TH SAPHIRA-REPO-MIGRATE 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-repo-migrate \- explicit legacy JSON to SQLite migration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-repo-migrate
.I REPO
.br
.B saphira-repo-migrate --reconcile
.RB [ --from-history ]
.I REPO
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-repo-migrate
builds a generation repository's
.I repository.db
once, explicitly: full APK census, carrier payload declarations,
cross-validation against
.I ownership.json
(owners map must match exactly), a full union collision check, then
atomic install plus a
.I migration.json
manifest. The JSON files are frozen read-only as evidence and never
consulted again; a missing
.I accounts.json
is recorded, never manufactured (its one historical exception is
.BR saphira-accounts-bootstrap (8)).
.B --reconcile
rebuilds current tables and verifies the eternal ledger (legitimate
drops tombstone loudly; tombstones are never deleted; unknown
history fails closed).
.B --from-history
re-derives tombstones, but only where complete append-only history
exists; on a current-view repository it refuses and points at the
archive. Bare signing never migrates anything silently. Must be run
as root; use sudo explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --reconcile
Rebuild and verify instead of fresh-migrating.
.TP
.B --from-history
Re-derive tombstones (append-only history only).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /out/stage4/packages/<generation>/$ARCH/repository.db
Created (migrate) or rebuilt (reconcile).
.TP
.I /out/stage4/packages/<generation>/$ARCH/migration.json
Migration manifest and input hashes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Migrated or reconciled.
.TP
.B 1
Refusal (already migrated, missing inputs, failed validation, held
lock) or not root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
sudo saphira-repo-migrate hatchling
.br
sudo saphira-repo-migrate --reconcile hatched
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira (7),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
.BR saphira-repo-state (8),
.BR saphira-accounts-bootstrap (8),
.BR ensure-identity (8),
.BR saphira-build (8)
